  --stored-auth-only                Never start interactive OAuth; use the
                                    shared store if present, otherwise fail with
                                    auth_required. Preferred for
                                    CI/non-interactive runs. No-op when the
                                    server does not require auth.
  --relogin                         Delete stored OAuth for this server URL from
                                    the shared store before connect (HTTP/SSE
                                    URL keys only); interactive login runs only
                                    if the server requires auth. Rejected for
                                    stdio (no URL-keyed store entry)
  --no-revoke                       Requires --relogin. Skips the RFC 7009
                                    revocation request that would otherwise end
                                    the grant at the authorization server when
                                    the local state is deleted. Also skipped
                                    when the server entry sets
                                    oauth.revokeOnClear to false.
  --wait-for-auth <sec>             Poll the OAuth state file until a token for
                                    --server-url appears (or the timeout
                                    elapses), then proceed as if
                                    --use-stored-auth were set. Use after
                                    handing off to a human to complete OAuth in
                                    a browser.
  --list-stored-auth                Print the server URLs that have a stored
                                    OAuth token (one JSON object on stdout) and
                                    exit. No server connection is made.
  --print-handoff                   Print a JSON handoff block (deepLink,
                                    portForwardCmd, oauthStatePath, apiToken)
                                    for --server-url and exit. No server
                                    connection is made.
  --completion <shell>              Print a shell completion script (bash, zsh,
                                    fish) on stdout and exit. No server
                                    connection is made.
  -h, --help                        display help for command
